{
  "_comment": [
    "Source: BattleMech Manual (BMM) p139, 'Mech Hit Location Table.",
    "p139 has exactly three columns, in this order: Left Side | Front/Rear | Right Side. It has no separate rear column.",
    "p139 row-to-roll mapping (columns: Left Side | Front/Rear | Right Side):",
    "  2 (critical - p139 footnote, p32) : Left Torso   | Center Torso | Right Torso",
    "  3                                : Left Leg     | Right Arm    | Right Leg",
    "  4                                : Left Arm     | Right Arm    | Right Arm",
    "  5                                : Left Arm     | Right Leg    | Right Arm",
    "  6                                : Left Leg     | Right Torso   | Right Leg",
    "  7                                : Left Torso   | Center Torso | Right Torso",
    "  8                                : Center Torso | Left Torso   | Center Torso",
    "  9                                : Right Torso  | Left Leg     | Left Torso",
    " 10                                : Right Arm    | Left Arm     | Left Arm",
    " 11                                : Right Leg    | Left Arm     | Left Leg",
    " 12                                : Head         | Head         | Head",
    "'front' is the p139 Front/Rear column; 'left' and 'right' are the p139 Left Side and Right Side columns (see tests/rules/combat/HitTables.test.js).",
    "'rear' is NOT a separate p139 column. Because the p139 middle column is labelled Front/Rear, rear attacks use the front locations; p44 (Transferring Damage) sends rear damage to the rear torso facing (for example, rear damage that hits a missing left leg transfers to the left rear torso). The rear table is therefore the front column with isRear:true on the three torso entries only: arms, legs and the head have no rear armour and must not carry isRear:true.",
    "Physical attacks (p139/p140) use 1D6 tables keyed by attack-direction column: 'left' | 'front' | 'right'. A rear attack uses the Front/Rear column, so the resolver maps 'rear' to 'front'.",
    "  punch = p140 'Mech Punch Location Table, biped (columns Left Side | Front/Rear | Right Side): 1 Left Torso|Left Arm|Right Torso; 2 Left Torso|Left Torso|Right Torso; 3 Center Torso|Center Torso|Center Torso; 4 Left Arm|Right Torso|Right Arm; 5 Left Arm|Right Arm|Right Arm; 6 Head|Head|Head.",
    "  kick = p139 'Mech Kick Location Table, biped (columns Left Side | Front/Rear | Right Side): 1-3 Left Leg|Right Leg|Right Leg; 4-6 Left Leg|Left Leg|Right Leg.",
    "The four-legged punch/kick columns (left/right front and rear legs) are not modelled: the unit model has no quad leg locations.",
    "The resolver rolls 1D6 for punch, kick, charge and DFA locations (charge and DFA use the punch table), and keeps the 2D6 standard p139 table only for physical-weapon attacks that use the standard table."
  ],
